.TH NHOPKG-SRC 8 "@RELEASEDATE@" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "Nhopkg Manual"
.SH NAME
nhopkg-src \- create, validate, and build source package projects for nhopkg
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nhopkg-src
\fB\-\-init\fR [\fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-meta\fR]
.br
.B nhopkg-src
\fB\-\-createpackage\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B nhopkg-src
\fB\-\-buildpackage\fR
.br
.B nhopkg-src
\fB\-\-validate\fR [\fIfile\fR]
.br
.B nhopkg-src
\fB\-\-get-source\fR \fIproject\fR [\fB\-\-ref\fR \fIref\fR]
.br
.B nhopkg-src
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
.B nhopkg-src
\fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBnhopkg-src\fR creates, validates, and builds source package projects for nhopkg.
It works with \fI.srcnho\fR files \(em flat tarballs containing the \fInhoid\fR metadata
file plus patches and extra files, which \fBnhopkg \-bv\fR uses to download, compile,
and install binary packages.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-\-init [\fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-meta\fR]
Create a new source package project interactively.
.br
If \fIname\fR is provided on the command line, it is used as the package name
(and project directory). Otherwise the tool prompts for it.
.br
Prompts are asked interactively with sensible defaults:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
Version (1.0)
.IP \(bu 4
Release (1)
.IP \(bu 4
Group (base, libs, ...; space-separated for multiple groups, Enter to skip)
.IP \(bu 4
Repository (extra; empty or Enter defaults to extra)
.IP \(bu 4
Description
.IP \(bu 4
Maintainer name (defaults to $USER)
.IP \(bu 4
Maintainer email (defaults to $USER@$HOSTNAME)
.IP \(bu 4
Packager
.IP \(bu 4
URL (project home page)
.IP \(bu 4
Download URL (Packageurl; tarball, git+<url>, svn+<url> or hg+<url>)
.IP \(bu 4
VCS reference (Packageref, required for git+, svn+ and hg+ sources)
.IP \(bu 4
Checksum (MD5, SHA256, SHA512 or BSUM; SHA256 by default; optional; can be downloaded automatically)
.IP \(bu 4
License
.IP \(bu 4
Architecture (set to machine architecture)
.IP \(bu 4
Provides / Conflicts (optional)
.RE
.P
When \fB\-\-meta\fR is used, only \fIPackage Name\fR, \fIPackage Version\fR,
\fIPackage Release\fR, \fIPackage Maintainer Name\fR, \fIPackage Maintainer
Email\fR, \fIPackage Group\fR, \fIRepository\fR, and \fITarget group name\fR
are prompted. All other fields are set automatically:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
License: CUSTOM
.IP \(bu 4
Architecture: any
.IP \(bu 4
URL: https://gitlab.com/neonatox-sources/<name>
.IP \(bu 4
Description: Metapackage for <name> group.
.IP \(bu 4
Packageurl: omitted (no source tarball)
.RE
.P
The target group's packages are resolved from repository metadata and written
as BuildDep and Dep(post) entries automatically. The resulting project can be
packaged and installed like any source package, but \fInbuild()\fR does nothing
and a \fIREADME.meta\fR is generated in the documentation directory.
.P
The project directory contains:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
\fInhoid\fR \(em the source recipe metadata file
.IP \(bu 4
\fIpatches/\fR \(em directory for patch files (*.patch, *.diff)
.IP \(bu 4
\fIothers/\fR \(em directory for extra files
.IP \(bu 4
\fIsources/\fR \(em downloaded tarballs (excluded from .srcnho)
.IP \(bu 4
\fIbuild/\fR \(em build artifacts (excluded from .srcnho)
.RE
.P
If the download URL has a known extension (.tar.gz, .tar.xz, .tar.bz2,
.tar.zst, .tgz, .tar, .zip), the tarball is downloaded to \fIsources/\fR.

.TP
.B \-\-createpackage [\fB\-\-force\fR]
Package the current project directory into a \fI.srcnho\fR file.
.br
The output file is named \fI<name>-<version>-<release>.srcnho\fR.
.br
\fB\-\-force\fR overwrites an existing output file without prompting.

.TP
.B \-\-buildpackage
Build the \fI.srcnho\fR package by running \fBnhopkg \-bv\fR with \fBsudo \-k\fR.
.br
The tool determines the expected .srcnho filename by reading the nhoid metadata
in the current directory. Always prompts for sudo credentials.

.TP
.B \-\-get-source \fIproject\fR [\fB\-\-ref\fR \fIref\fR]
Clone a source project from the \fBNHOPKG_GIT_SOURCES\fR repository.
.br
The project is cloned into a subdirectory named after the project. If
\fB\-\-ref\fR is given, it is passed to git as a tag, branch, or commit
reference. After cloning, the standard \fIpatches/\fR and \fIothers/\fR
directories are created so the project is ready for editing and packaging.
.br
The repository URL is built as \fI${NHOPKG_GIT_SOURCES}/${project}.git\fR.

.TP
.B \-\-validate [\fIfile\fR]
Validate a .srcnho package or the nhoid file in the current directory.
.br
If no file is given, validates \fInhoid\fR in the current directory.
.br
Checks performed:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
Extension is .srcnho (or current dir has nhoid)
.IP \(bu 4
Tarball extractable
.IP \(bu 4
nhoid file exists and has correct header (%NHO-0.5)
.IP \(bu 4
Name, Version, Release fields are present and non-empty
.IP \(bu 4
nbuild() function exists and is not noemptyfuncs
.IP \(bu 4
ninstall() (or ninstall_<part>() variants) exist and are not noemptyfuncs
.IP \(bu 4
npostinstall() and npostremove() may be noemptyfuncs
.IP \(bu 4
All split parts defined in Parts: have corresponding ninstall_<part>()
.IP \(bu 4
No duplicate function definitions
.IP \(bu 4
Warns if a checksum (MD5, SHA256, SHA512, BSUM) is missing for tarball sources
.IP \(bu 4
Warns if Packageref is missing for VCS sources (git+, svn+, hg+)
.IP \(bu 4
Warns if Description is empty
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-meta
With \fB\-\-init\fR, create a metapackage project. No source tarball or
download URL is required; package metadata is filled automatically and the
target group's packages are resolved as dependencies.
.TP
.B \-\-force
With \fB\-\-createpackage\fR, overwrite existing .srcnho file without prompting.
.TP
.B \-\-ref \fIref\fR
Git reference (tag, branch, or commit) for \fB\-\-get-source\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Each \fB\-\-init\fR prompt can be pre-answered by exporting the matching
environment variable; when the variable is already set the prompt is skipped.
The recognized variables are \fIPKG_NAME\fR, \fIPKG_VERSION\fR,
\fIPKG_RELEASE\fR, \fIPKG_MAINTAINER_NAME\fR, \fIPKG_MAINTAINER_EMAIL\fR,
\fIPKG_GROUP\fR, \fIPKG_REPOSITORY\fR, \fIPKG_LICENSE\fR, \fIPKG_ARCH\fR,
\fIPKG_URL\fR, \fIPKG_DESCRIPTION\fR, \fIPKG_PACKAGEURL\fR,
\fIPKG_PACKAGEREF\fR, \fIPKG_HASH_TYPE\fR, \fIPKG_DOWNLOAD\fR,
\fIPKG_META_GROUP\fR (with \fB\-\-meta\fR), \fIPKG_SPLIT\fR,
\fIPKG_PROVIDES\fR, and \fIPKG_CONFLICTS\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a new project
.B nhopkg-src \-\-init myapp
.TP
Package the project
.B nhopkg-src \-\-createpackage
.TP
Build the package
.B nhopkg-src \-\-buildpackage
.TP
Validate the result
.B nhopkg-src \-\-validate myapp-1.0-1.srcnho
.TP
Clone a source project
.B nhopkg-src \-\-get-source gcc
.TP
Clone a source project with a specific branch
.B nhopkg-src \-\-get-source gcc \-\-ref n2027
.SH FILES
.TP
.I nhoid
Source recipe metadata file in the project directory.
.TP
.I patches/*.patch, patches/*.diff
Patch files applied during build.
.TP
.I others/*
Extra files included in the .srcnho (e.g. desktop files, icons).
.TP
.I sources/
Downloaded tarballs (excluded from .srcnho).
.TP
.I build/
Build artifacts (excluded from .srcnho).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nhopkg (8),
.BR nhopkg.conf (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Jaime Gil de Sagredo Luna <jaimegildesagredo@gmail.com>
